# SDK releases

For release or publication work, read `RELEASING.md` first.

- A release is complete only when its annotated remote tag, PyPI wheel and
  source distribution, and published GitHub Release all exist and agree.
- Build from the clean, tested release commit; push its annotated version tag
  before uploading the exact checked artifacts to PyPI.
- Verify the `GitHub release` workflow succeeded and the latest GitHub Release
  agrees with PyPI. A tag alone is not a GitHub Release entry.
- Repair missing entries using the documented workflow dispatch. Never move a
  published tag, rebuild an existing version, or bypass artifact verification.
